course: dictionary
lesson: 1319
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence around it tells you which one to use. Calculate is a good example. In maths, «Calculate the total» means work out the answer using numbers. In a story, a calculating villain is someone who plans cleverly and coldly to get what they want.
explain: Look for clues in the words around it. Numbers, sums, and questions about how many or how much point to the number meaning. Words about plans, cruelty or getting your own way point to the other meaning. Ask yourself: what is this sentence about?
explain: Calculate can also mean to judge by thinking carefully, as in «before you calculate, ask: which numbers are about the thing the question asks?» Here it means think carefully about what matters. Swap your meaning into the sentence and check it still makes sense.
fact: Calculate means to work out an amount or answer using numbers.
fact: Calculated can mean planned on purpose, as in «a calculated risk».
fact: Calculating can describe someone who is clever in a cold, selfish way.
fact: In the 1840s, Ada Lovelace wrote notes for a calculating machine that Charles Babbage designed but never finished.
fact: In 1974 Stephen Hawking calculated that black holes should slowly leak tiny amounts of energy.
exercise: «Calculate the total of 12 and 7.» What does calculate mean here? | Guess without thinking | *Work out the answer using numbers | Draw a picture of the numbers | Read the numbers aloud
exercise: «The villain was calculating, always planning how to get the treasure for himself.» What does calculating suggest? | Kind and generous | Tired from walking | Very loud and silly | *Clever in a cold, selfish way
exercise: «He took a calculated risk and it paid off.» What does calculated mean? | Dropped by accident | *Planned on purpose after careful thought | Sung very quietly | Written down in a list
test: «Before you calculate, ask which numbers matter.» What does calculate mean here? | Break something by accident | Count the people in the room | *Judge by thinking carefully | Sing a song
test: Ada Lovelace's notes showed steps for a machine to calculate Bernoulli numbers. What does calculate mean in this sentence? | Paint a picture | Feel very sad | Plan a cruel trick | *Work out using numbers
exam: «The calculating queen plotted to steal the crown.» What does calculating mean here? | Sorting things into piles | Happy and excited | *Clever in a cold, selfish way | Good at drawing pictures
